--- a/docs/libssh2_session_callback_set2.md
+++ b/docs/libssh2_session_callback_set2.md
@@ -102,6 +102,28 @@ The callback returns the number of bytes read, or -1 for error. The special
 return code **-EAGAIN** can be returned to signal that the read was aborted
 to prevent getting blocked and it needs to be called again.

+## LIBSSH2_CALLBACK_USERAUTH_BANNER
+
+Called once for each valid SSH_MSG_USERAUTH_BANNER received before
+authentication succeeds, after transport integrity and strict KEX checks.
+Packets with an invalid MAC never trigger this callback, even if accepted by
+LIBSSH2_CALLBACK_MACERROR. Banners are still queued and processed normally.
+Multiple, including identical, banners can trigger this callback.
+
+The prototype of the callback:
+
+~~~c
+void banner(LIBSSH2_SESSION *session, const char *message,
+            size_t message_length, const char *language,
+            size_t language_length, void **abstract);
+~~~
+
+The message and language pointers are borrowed, are not necessarily
+NUL-terminated, and remain valid only until the callback returns. Copy the
+explicit-length byte ranges before retaining them. The callback runs
+synchronously while the packet is processed and must not block or reenter
+authentication or transport processing on the same session.
+
 ## LIBSSH2_CALLBACK_AUTHAGENT

